Imagine you have two separate topological patches on your quantum grid, each protected by its own surface code.

23:23.820 --> 23:28.160
Lattice surgery allows you to temporarily alter the boundary measurements between them,

23:28.640 --> 23:34.800
essentially unzipping the edges of the two codes and stitching them together into one larger unified surface code,

23:35.320 --> 23:37.440
and it does this completely fault-tolerantly.

